{
  "info": {
    "name": "Package Registry Service (Team 14)",
    "description": "Registry of client packages, their package-local Tamagotchi stat definitions, and Monster Raid configuration.\n\nOwner: IsStephy. Default port: 8088.\n\nEvery request goes through the gateway in the shared stack: the gateway verifies the player's token, drops it, and forwards `X-Gateway-Key` (proving the request came through it) plus `X-User-Id` (the player). This service never verifies tokens and answers 401 to anything without a valid `X-Gateway-Key`, except /health and /docs.\n\nThis collection talks to the service directly, so it sends those two headers itself - it plays the gateway. Set the `gatewayKey` variable to the GATEWAY_KEY in your .env (the default, `change_me`, matches .env.example). To go through the real gateway with real logins, use collections/gateway.postman_collection.json.\n\n`GET /packages` and `GET /packages/{id}` need no player, but still the gateway key. Admin and package-moderator roles are checked by this service against its own data.\n\nThe first admin is seeded from PACKAGE_REGISTRY_INITIAL_ADMIN_USER_ID (admin-1 by default), which is the `adminId` this collection uses.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8088"
    },
    {
      "key": "packageId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "raidConfigId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "moderatorId",
      "value": "mod-1"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminId",
      "value": "admin-1"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "u-owner-1"
    },
    {
      "key": "guildId",
      "value": "guild-demo-1"
    },
    {
      "key": "noGuildConfigId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "gatewayKey",
      "value": "change_me"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Liveness check. Returns { status: ok, service: package-registry-service }."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Grant Admin",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// 200 the first time, 409 on later runs - both mean admin-2 exists.",
              "pm.test('200 OK or 409 already an admin', function () {",
              "    pm.expect([200, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Gateway-Key",
            "value": "{{gatewayKey}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-User-Id",
            "value": "{{adminId}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"admin-2\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admins",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "admins"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Grants global admin status to a second user. The caller must already be an admin - the first one is seeded from PACKAGE_REGISTRY_INITIAL_ADMIN_USER_ID at startup, which is why this request is sent as adminId."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Register Package",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('returns packageId and status', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('packageId');",
              "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('active');",
              "});",
              "// Save the id so the rest of the collection can use it.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('packageId', body.packageId);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Gateway-Key",
            "value": "{{gatewayKey}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-User-Id",
            "value": "{{adminId}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Tamagotchi Go Classic\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"description\": \"Base package with hunger and happiness stats\",\n  \"moderatorIds\": [\"{{moderatorId}}\"]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/packages",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "packages"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Registers a new client package. New packages start with status `active` and empty stat definitions."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Packages",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('returns an array', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Gateway-Key",
            "value": "{{gatewayKey}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/packages",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "packages"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Lists every registered package, for discovery - a caller no longer needs to already know a packageId."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Update Stat Definitions",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('stat definitions were stored', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().statDefinitions).to.have.property('hunger');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Gateway-Key",
            "value": "{{gatewayKey}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-User-Id",
            "value": "{{moderatorId}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"statDefinitions\": {\n    \"hunger\": {\n      \"maxValue\": 100,\n      \"bonusThreshold\": 80,\n      \"bonusMultiplier\": 1.2\n    },\n    \"happiness\": {\n      \"maxValue\": 100,\n      \"bonusThreshold\": 60,\n      \"bonusMultiplier\": 1.1\n    }\n  }\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/packages/{{packageId}}/stat-definitions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "packages",
            "{{packageId}}",
            "stat-definitions"
          ]
        },
        "description": "A moderator defines this package's local Tamagotchi stats.\n\nPackages are intentionally non-normalized - another package may define energy/mood/discipline instead. Battle Service reads these definitions to compute package-specific combat bonuses, so each one is validated: maxValue > 0, bonusThreshold between 0 and maxValue, bonusMultiplier > 0."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Package",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('returns the contract fields', function () {",
              "    const body = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('packageId', 'name', 'version', 'status', 'statDefinitions');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Gateway-Key",
            "value": "{{gatewayKey}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/packages/{{packageId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "packages",
            "{{packageId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Retrieves a package's details, including its current stat definitions. This is the endpoint Battle Service and Tamagotchi Service pull from."
      },
      "response": []
    },
